course: dictionary
lesson: 12085
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The clues in the sentence show you which meaning the writer means. «Mum pegged the wet shirts on the clothesline in the sunshine.» Pegs and shirts are clues that a clothesline is a rope or wire for drying washing.
explain: «The defender gave a clothesline to the striker, and the referee blew the whistle.» Here clothesline is a verb, and it means knocking someone over with an outstretched arm across the neck or chest. The words defender, striker and referee are clues that this is a sport word, not a washing word.
explain: To check your meaning, put it into the sentence. If the sentence still makes sense, you have probably chosen well. If it sounds silly, look at the clues again or try the other meaning.
fact: A clothesline is a rope or wire on which washed clothes are hung to dry.
fact: Clothes dry on the clothesline because water evaporates in the sun and wind.
fact: In sport, «clothesline» can be a verb meaning to knock someone over by hitting them across the neck or chest with an outstretched arm.
fact: A clothesline tackle in sport is dangerous and against the rules.
fact: In Australia, a rotary clothesline, often called a Hills Hoist, is used to hang out the washing.
exercise: «Dad hung the sheets on the clothesline to dry.» What is a clothesline here? | A long line of people waiting for a bus | A line drawn across the pitch | *A rope or wire for drying washing | A thin string for flying a kite
exercise: «The defender gave a clothesline to the striker, and the referee blew the whistle.» What does clothesline mean here? | *To knock someone over with an arm across the neck or chest | To shout very loudly | To hang washing out to dry | To draw a straight line on paper
exercise: Why do clothes dry on the clothesline? | The clothesline stops the rain | The clothes shrink when they are hung up | The rope is made of wood | *Water evaporates in the sun and wind
test: What is a clothesline? | *A rope or wire on which washing is hung to dry | A long line of ants | A type of sports ball | A kind of bicycle
test: «Ben was given a red card for a clothesline in the football match.» What does the sentence tell you about a clothesline in sport? | It means a long line of players | *It is dangerous and against the rules | It is a safe and fair move | It helps the washing dry
exam: «The coach told the players that a clothesline tackle is dangerous and against the rules.» What does this sentence tell you about a clothesline tackle? | It is a kind of rope for the goal | It is safe and allowed in the game | *It is dangerous and against the rules | It is a way to dry the kit
